{
 "about": "Shared rules for what another member's content may become in Tin Hat (security review 2026-10-26: H1, H2). Byte-identical copies: desktop crates/app/src/testvectors/member-content.json (replayed by richtext.rs, viewer.rs and tools/link-gate-test.mjs on LinkGate.qml), web src/features/chat/lib/testvectors/member-content.json. html: 'in' = a member's formatted_body; after sanitising, 'text' = the visible text (text nodes, entities decoded), 'hrefs' = every link's href (WHATWG-serialised, as new URL(x).href), 'absent' = substrings that must not survive (case-insensitive); 'qt' = the desktop's exact output (Qt rich text dialect: font->span, del/strike->s, details->div, summary->p>b). The rules: the Matrix tag subset; img -> its alt text (never loaded); script/style/iframe/svg/math/audio/video/mx-reply/... dropped with their contents; other tags keep their text; only href (links rule), ol start (digits), code class language-*, data-mx-color/color/data-mx-bg-color #hex (-> style), data-mx-spoiler survive; a link whose text names another host (the claims rule below) is followed by ' (<href host>)'; a link with a user name before the host is no link. links: the one link gate for everything the apps open (web: core/openlink.ts safeExternalUrl; desktop: richtext.rs link_verdict + LinkGate.qml): trim C0/space at both ends; a control character or DEL left inside -> bad-char; no 'scheme:' -> no-scheme; scheme not http/https/mailto/steam -> scheme; steam needs '//' and something after it (no space), and 'ask': 'steam' = it opens only after an 'Open in Steam?' confirmation (every other app scheme is refused); http(s) needs '//' and a host (a space in the host -> bad-char, a user name/password -> userinfo, none -> no-host); 'why' is the desktop's word (the web only checks 'open'); 'as' = what an allowed link opens (a mailto keeps only its subject, body and cc fields, names case-insensitive, no fragment). Cases where Qt and a browser parse differently (a backslash, 'https:host', 'https:///host') are not here: the desktop refuses them, the web normalises them with new URL. viewer: attachment mime (parameters dropped, case-insensitive) -> the extension it is opened as (null = Save as only); inline = decoded in the bubble. sniff: the bytes (hex, first bytes) are that extension's type. claims: the host a link's text claims — the note after a link and the question at the click, both apps. Only for an http(s) link with a host that is not matrix.to (a mention pill's text is a display name). Invisible characters (\\p{Cf}, \\p{Default_Ignorable_Code_Point}) are dropped; the text is split at white space; each word loses its leading and trailing characters that are not letters or digits (\\p{L}\\p{N}); a word claims a host when (a) it has a scheme ('://', http/https), starts with 'www.' or has a path ('/'), and its host (http://<word> unless it has a scheme) is dotted with a last label of >= 2 ASCII letters or xn--, or (b) it is a bare dotted name whose last label is a top-level domain in testvectors/tlds.txt (IANA's list, byte-identical in both repos, case-insensitive). Hosts compare lower-case without a trailing dot or a leading www.; the first claim other than the link's host counts; 'claim' = that host, null = none. claimExclude: as BARE dotted names (no scheme, no www., no '/') words whose last label is one of these do not claim (code-file names: README.md, main.py, lib.rs, run.sh); zip and mov still do. ownSounds: a stored sound URL is this server's own upload only as <base>/soundboard/clip?id=[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128} or <base>/soundboard/file/<one name: [A-Za-z0-9_-] then [A-Za-z0-9_.-], at most 128> (the base compared case-insensitively; anything else — another path, a query, %2e, %2f, %5c in any case — is not). soundRoute: how a stored sound URL plays, in this order: 'myinstants' (it starts with '/' or contains 'myinstants.com/') -> play = <base>/soundboard/clip?url=<pctEncode(url)> (RFC 3986 unreserved kept, every other byte %XX upper case); 'own' (the ownSounds shapes under <base>) -> play = the URL itself; 'foreign' (another Tin Hat server's upload: https://<host>[:443]/api/soundboard/clip?id=[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128} with no other query, or https://<host>[:443]/api/soundboard/file/<[A-Za-z0-9_-][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,127}>; the host a dotted DNS name other than <base>'s host, not an IP address; no user name, no other port, no fragment, no %2e/%2f/%5c in any case, no backslash or white space) -> play = <base>/soundboard/clip?url=<pctEncode(url)> (our own server fetches it; never directly); else 'refuse' (no play).",
